{"uid":"e00b637568f2f443","name":"QA 2114","fullName":"QA #2114 on ubuntu1804-container","historyId":"2114@ubuntu1804-container","time":{"start":1794280757000,"stop":1794280758000,"duration":1000},"description":"PCP QA Test No. 2114\n\n\n\nCheck for memory leaks on the error paths of the derived metrics parser,\n\nand in the teardown of a derived metric holding a compiled regex.\n\n\n\nCompanion test qa/2113 checks the diagnostics from the same expressions.\n\n\n\nNote the expressions are deliberately bundled into one config file, and\n\nthe last one is deliberately harmless.  The parser keeps its most recent\n\nallocations in file-scope statics (np, specmeta) and in bison's\n\nderive_lval, so the last thing a failed parse leaks is still reachable\n\nat exit and valgrind reports it as \"still reachable\", not \"definitely\n\nlost\".  It only becomes definitely lost once a later parse overwrites\n\nthose pointers ... so every expression here needs another one after it,\n\nand one expression per run would prove nothing.\n\n\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 Red Hat.  All Rights Reserved.\n\n\n\n","descriptionHtml":"<p>PCP QA Test No. 2114</p>\n<p>Check for memory leaks on the error paths of the derived metrics parser,</p>\n<p>and in the teardown of a derived metric holding a compiled regex.</p>\n<p>Companion test qa/2113 checks the diagnostics from the same expressions.</p>\n<p>Note the expressions are deliberately bundled into one config file, and</p>\n<p>the last one is deliberately harmless.  The parser keeps its most recent</p>\n<p>allocations in file-scope statics (np, specmeta) and in bison's</p>\n<p>derive_lval, so the last thing a failed parse leaks is still reachable</p>\n<p>at exit and valgrind reports it as &quot;still reachable&quot;, not &quot;definitely</p>\n<p>lost&quot;.  It only becomes definitely lost once a later parse overwrites</p>\n<p>those pointers ... so every expression here needs another one after it,</p>\n<p>and one expression per run would prove nothin